2.chebyshevs  Inequality:

let X is any continuous random variable .
X~ Non-GD(mean,sd )then 
When data is not normal, we cannot use the empirical rule.
So we use Chebyshev’s inequality.

(mean-k*sigma)<X<=(mean+k*sigma)>1-1/k^2

(mean - kσ) < X ≤ (mean + kσ)
Probability ≥ 1 - 1/k²
μ (mean) = average
σ (sigma) = standard deviation
k = number of standard deviations
k-->range of SD 

